# Platform UI Presentation Quality

See `lib/platform-presentation-quality/`.

## Never show in visible UI

- Raw ISO-8601 timestamps (`2026-07-31T02:42:07…+00:00`)
- Raw database enums / API status codes (`active`, `ready`, `enabled`, `not_ready`)
- Raw `snake_case` or `camelCase` technical codes as primary labels
- Raw translation keys
- English status fallbacks in Norwegian (or other non-English) UI
- CSS `text-transform: capitalize` as a status “fix”

## Required contracts

1. **Dates** — use `formatPlatformDateTimeFull` / `Short` / `DateOnly` / `RelativeTime` / `Duration` with active locale + authoritative timezone (`resolveAuthoritativeTimeZone`). Never `toISOString()` for display.
2. **Statuses** — use `resolvePlatformStatusLabel` / `getPlatformStatusPresentation` with central `platform.presentationQuality.statuses` maps. Severity is separate (`resolvePlatformStatusSeverity`). Capitalization comes from the translated label.
3. **No duplicated per-component status switches by language.**
4. **Unknown status** — controlled fallback label; never the raw code in production.
5. **Null vs missing** — do not map every null to “Not available” when the authoritative relation shows “not linked” / “not configured”.
6. **Consistency** — the same customer may legitimately show different statuses across delivery, activation, and runtime cards (different RPCs / state machines). Always show the card scope note; never invent a unified status by mutating customer data.
7. **Tests** — presentation-quality tests under `lib/platform-presentation-quality/**` are required before release of Platform customer presentation changes.

## Allowed

- Minimal read-only adapter changes when a card uses the wrong data source
- Locale parity for all active locales (`LOCALES` in `lib/i18n/config.ts`)

## Forbidden in this surface

- Customer data writes, license/entitlement/delivery/domain/install/runtime mutations, migrations, dependency/lockfile changes — to “make cards look green”
